{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>But you shall keep My statutes.</b> Why was it necessary to say אתם — 'you'? To exclude the other nations: even if they wished to keep the commandments, they cannot. And so our Rabbis, blessed be their memory, said: a son of Noah who observed Shabbat is liable to death, and this is the sense of ושמרתם אתם — 'you shall keep' — none are obligated in the keeping of the commandments but you."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:31.596572359Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}